From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 03:31:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msxml3: Keep a unary minus to its operand, and take a single
 one before MSXML 4.0.

A unary step left its second operand at zero, where a binary step has
it, so evaluating a unary minus evaluated the first step of the
expression again, pushed what it gave, and negated that.  -1 = -1 was
false, and so was -1 < 0.

As measured on Windows 11, MSXML 6 takes any number of unary minuses in
a row, while MSXML 3 takes a single one: --1 and - -1 fail to compile
there, -(-1) and 1--1 do not.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/msxml3/tests/domdoc.c b/dlls/msxml3/tests/domdoc.c
index 91e42731a95..8201946a64c 100644
--- a/dlls/msxml3/tests/domdoc.c
+++ b/dlls/msxml3/tests/domdoc.c
@@ -5454,6 +5454,10 @@ static void test_XPath(void)
         { "//elem[@a <= \"c\"]", "" },
         { "//elem[@a = \"c\"]", "E3.E2.D1" },
         { "//elem[@a != 0]", "E1.E2.D1 E2.E2.D1 E3.E2.D1" },
+        /* a unary minus */
+        { "//elem[@min = -1]", "E1.E2.D1" },
+        { "//elem[-@max = -20]", "E2.E2.D1" },
+        { "//elem[-(-@min) = -10]", "E4.E2.D1" },
         { NULL },
     };
 
diff --git a/dlls/msxml3/xpath.c b/dlls/msxml3/xpath.c
index e5739604f3c..738318c3a37 100644
--- a/dlls/msxml3/xpath.c
+++ b/dlls/msxml3/xpath.c
@@ -786,6 +786,7 @@ static void xpath_push_unary_step(struct xpath_parser_context *ctxt, enum xpath_
 
     step->op = op;
     step->ch1 = ch;
+    step->ch2 = -1;
     step->value = value;
     step->value2 = value2;
 }
@@ -1900,6 +1901,9 @@ static void xpath_compile_unary_expr(struct xpath_parser_context *ctxt)
     xpath_parse_skipspaces(ctxt);
     while (xpath_parse_cmp(ctxt, L"-"))
     {
+        /* MSXML before 4.0 takes a single minus: --1 does not compile, -(-1) does */
+        if (found && ctxt->context && ctxt->context->properties && ctxt->context->properties->version < MSXML4)
+            return xpath_parser_context_set_error(ctxt, XPATH_EXPR_ERROR);
         minus = 1 - minus;
         found = true;
         xpath_parse_skipspaces(ctxt);
